#!/bin/sh
# One 60 s s2idle suspend on battery with before/after sleep counters, for the
# standby bisect boots (compose-standby-bisect-dtb.sh). Run it detached, as
# root, with the screen off and the cable pulled:
#   systemd-run --unit rog5-standby-bisect --collect \
#       /usr/local/sbin/rog5-standby-bisect-measure [OPTIONS]
#   journalctl -u rog5-standby-bisect; cat /var/lib/rog5-standby-bisect/*/summary.txt
#
# Options:
#   --secs=60        suspend length (RTC wake alarm; never suspends without one)
#   --wait=900       wait this long for USB power to go away (cable pulled)
#   --no-battmgr     noadsp boot: no battery/USB telemetry; the caller vouches
#                    the cable is out (checks Type-C/USB power cannot be read)
#   --arm-vx         before suspending, send the AOP violator-log request
#                    {class: lpm_mon, type: cxpc, ...} through the debug module
#                    rog5-aop-qmp (tools/standby_probe; must be loaded). A QMP
#                    write: off by default (Sol: baseline without monitoring).
#   --ddr-log-off    optional stock-difference test: send
#                    {class: ddr, res: ddr_log, val: 0} through rog5-aop-qmp.
#                    Stock 5.4 registers this as the BIMC clock of clk-aop-qmp
#                    but no lahaina DT node consumes it and ROG5's FDT lacks
#                    qcom,clk-stop-bimc-log, so stock never sends it at
#                    runtime; val 0 only turns AOP DDR logging off. val 1 is
#                    never sent.
#
# APSS sleep: qcom_stats "apss" is SMEM item 631, which only the downstream
# kernel's rpmh_master_stat.c fills (from its LPM driver); under mainline it is
# never allocated and reads empty. The trial is judged by the time
# timekeeping stayed frozen in s2idle (boot clock minus monotonic clock, both
# before and after) and by the s2idle requests of the cluster's deepest genpd
# state (cluster-sleep-1, APSS off with the RSC sleep handshake). Both are the
# software view: hardware collapse shows only in the RPMh/DDR counters.
#
# Reads only: /sys/kernel/debug/qcom_stats/* (AOP message RAM and SMEM),
# /proc/uptime, /proc/timer_list ("now at"), the cluster genpd idle_states,
# power_supply attributes, suspend_stats, wakeup_sources, /proc/interrupts,
# remoteproc state, and rog5-sleep-blockers/vx and vx_raw when that module is
# loaded (AOP message RAM reads). It never reads rog5-sleep-blockers/votes
# (rpmh_read of resources this kernel never wrote hung the RSC and reset the
# phone), rog5-aop-qmp/ddr_votes or ddr_raw (each read sends a QMP message),
# the display RSC (0xaf20000) or /sys/kernel/debug/dri/*/DP-*.
# It stops no service. It writes: the RTC wake alarm (rtcwake), the suspend
# request, /run/rog5-stay-awake while it runs (so rog5-sleep-policy does not
# suspend on its own; removed afterwards if this script created it), progress
# lines to /dev/kmsg, and its result directory.
set -u
PATH=${ROG5_BISECT_TEST_BIN:+$ROG5_BISECT_TEST_BIN:}/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
export LC_ALL=C
secs=60 wait_s=900 battmgr=1 arm_vx=0 ddr_log_off=0
for arg in "$@"; do
	case $arg in
		--secs=*) secs=${arg#*=} ;;
		--wait=*) wait_s=${arg#*=} ;;
		--no-battmgr) battmgr=0 ;;
		--arm-vx) arm_vx=1 ;;
		--ddr-log-off) ddr_log_off=1 ;;
		*) sed -n '2,32p' "$0" >&2; exit 2 ;;
	esac
done
for value in "$secs" "$wait_s"; do
	case $value in ''|*[!0-9]*|0?*) echo 'decimal option expected (no leading zero)' >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
done
[ "$secs" -ge 20 ] && [ "$secs" -le 3600 ] || { echo '--secs must be 20..3600' >&2; exit 2; }
[ "$(id -u)" = 0 ] || { echo 'run as root' >&2; exit 1; }

stats=${ROG5_BISECT_STATS:-/sys/kernel/debug/qcom_stats}
bat=${ROG5_BISECT_BAT:-/sys/class/power_supply/qcom-battmgr-bat}
usb=${ROG5_BISECT_USB:-/sys/class/power_supply/qcom-battmgr-usb/online}
dpms=${ROG5_BISECT_DPMS:-/sys/class/drm/card1-DSI-1/dpms}
vxdir=/sys/kernel/debug/rog5-sleep-blockers
qmp=/sys/kernel/debug/rog5-aop-qmp/send
stay=${ROG5_BISECT_STAY:-/run/rog5-stay-awake}
succ_file=${ROG5_BISECT_SUCCESS:-/sys/power/suspend_stats/success}
dir=${ROG5_BISECT_OUT:-/var/lib/rog5-standby-bisect}/$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)
mkdir -p "$dir" || exit 1
created_stay=0
log() { printf '%s %s\n' "$(date -u +%FT%TZ)" "$*" | tee -a "$dir/log.txt"; printf 'rog5-standby-bisect: %s\n' "$*" >/dev/kmsg 2>/dev/null; }
cleanup() { [ "$created_stay" = 0 ] || rm -f "$stay"; }
trap cleanup EXIT
trap 'exit 130' INT TERM HUP

[ -d "$stats" ] || { log 'FAIL no qcom_stats (load qcom_stats)'; exit 1; }
rd() { v=; read -r v <"$1" 2>/dev/null || v=; printf '%s' "${v:-NA}"; }
uptime_file=${ROG5_BISECT_UPTIME:-/proc/uptime}
timer_list=${ROG5_BISECT_TIMER_LIST:-/proc/timer_list}
cluster=${ROG5_BISECT_CLUSTER:-/sys/kernel/debug/pm_genpd/power-domain-cpu-cluster0/idle_states}
boot() { cut -d ' ' -f 1 "$uptime_file"; }
# Seconds timekeeping has been frozen since boot: boot clock (/proc/uptime)
# minus the monotonic clock (/proc/timer_list "now at N nsecs"), 10 ms steps.
# Awake it is about 0 and may read slightly negative (uptime is rounded down
# and read first); only the before/after difference is used.
frozen() {
	b=$(boot) m=$(sed -n 's/^now at \([0-9]*\) nsecs$/\1/p' "$timer_list" | head -n 1)
	case $b in ''|.*|*.*.*|*[!0-9.]*) echo NA; return ;; esac
	case $m in ''|*[!0-9]*) echo NA; return ;; esac
	awk -v b="$b" -v m="$m" 'BEGIN { printf "%.2f\n", b - m / 1e9 }'
}
# usage, rejected and s2idle counts of the cluster's deepest idle state (the
# last row). genpd counts an s2idle request before PSCI runs; a refused PSCI
# call moves one usage to rejected but leaves the s2idle count: software
# evidence of APSS-off requests, not of hardware residency.
cluster_counts() {
	awk 'NR > 1 && $1 ~ /^S[0-9]+$/ { u = $3; r = $4; v = $7 }
		END { if (u ~ /^[0-9]+$/ && r ~ /^[0-9]+$/ && v ~ /^[0-9]+$/) print u, r, v; else print "NA NA NA" }' \
		"$cluster" 2>/dev/null || echo 'NA NA NA'
}

# -- preconditions: rog5-sleep-policy held off, s2idle, display off, on battery
[ -e "$stay" ] || {
	: >"$stay" || { log 'FAIL cannot create the stay-awake file'; exit 1; }
	created_stay=1
}
case " $(rd "${ROG5_BISECT_MEM_SLEEP:-/sys/power/mem_sleep}") " in *' [s2idle] '*) ;; *) log 'FAIL s2idle is not the selected mem_sleep'; exit 1 ;; esac
[ "$(rd "$dpms")" = Off ] || { log "FAIL the phone panel is not off (dpms $(rd "$dpms"))"; exit 1; }
for c in ${ROG5_BISECT_DRM:-/sys/class/drm}/card*-DP-*; do
	[ "$(rd "$c/enabled")" != enabled ] || { log "FAIL external display ${c##*/} is enabled"; exit 1; }
done
if [ "$battmgr" = 1 ]; then
	[ -r "$usb" ] || { log 'FAIL no battmgr USB supply (noadsp boot? use --no-battmgr)'; exit 1; }
	t=0
	while :; do
		case $(rd "$usb") in
			0) break ;;
			1) ;;
			*) log 'FAIL cannot read the USB power state'; exit 1 ;;
		esac
		[ "$t" -lt "$wait_s" ] || { log 'FAIL USB power never went away (pull the cable)'; exit 1; }
		[ "$t" != 0 ] || log 'waiting for the USB cable to be pulled'
		sleep 5; t=$((t + 5))
	done
	sleep 10
else
	[ ! -e "$usb" ] || { log 'FAIL --no-battmgr but battmgr is present'; exit 1; }
	# No VBUS reading without the ADSP; a live NCM link means the cable is in.
	t=0
	while [ "$(rd /sys/class/net/usb0/carrier)" = 1 ]; do
		[ "$t" -lt "$wait_s" ] || { log 'FAIL the USB gadget link is still up (pull the cable)'; exit 1; }
		[ "$t" != 0 ] || log 'waiting for the USB cable to be pulled (usb0 carrier)'
		sleep 5; t=$((t + 5))
	done
fi

# -- snapshots (read-only)
qstats() {
	for f in "$stats"/*; do
		[ -f "$f" ] || continue
		case ${f##*/} in ddr_stats) continue ;; esac
		text=$(tr '\n' ' ' <"$f") || return 1
		printf '%s %s\n' "${f##*/}" "$text"
	done
}
# Per-row count and tick deltas of ddr_stats, keyed by row name: the driver
# omits frequency rows whose count is still 0, so rows can appear.
ddr_deltas() {
	awk -F '\t' '
	function decode(  i, x) {
		key = $1; sub(/:$/, "", key); count = 0; ticks = 0
		for (i = 2; i <= NF; i++) {
			split($i, x, ":")
			if (x[1] == "count") count = x[2] + 0
			if (x[1] == "Duration (ticks)") ticks = x[2] + 0
		}
	}
	FNR == NR { decode(); c[key] = count; d[key] = ticks; next }
	{ decode(); printf "%s\t%.0f\t%.0f\n", key, count - c[key], ticks - d[key] }
	' "$dir/ddr.before" "$dir/ddr.after"
}
# Count and seconds delta of one qcom_stats entry, or "NA NA".
qdelta() {
	join "$dir/qstats.before" "$dir/qstats.after" | awk -v name="$1" '$1 == name { n = 0
		for (i = 2; i <= NF; i++) { if ($i == "Count:") c[n] = $(i + 1); if ($i == "Duration:") { d[n] = $(i + 1); n++ } }
		if (n == 2) { printf "%d %.1f\n", c[1] - c[0], (d[1] - d[0]) / 19200000; found = 1 } }
		END { if (!found) print "NA NA" }'
}
battery() {
	for a in status capacity charge_counter voltage_now current_now temp; do
		printf '%s=%s\n' "$a" "$(rd "$bat/$a")"
	done
}
# N current_now/voltage_now samples 1 s apart; prints mean mA and V.
sample_current() {
	i=0 n=$1 out=$2
	: >"$out"
	while [ "$i" -lt "$n" ]; do
		printf '%s %s %s\n' "$(boot)" "$(rd "$bat/current_now")" "$(rd "$bat/voltage_now")" >>"$out"
		i=$((i + 1)); sleep 1
	done
	awk '$2 ~ /^-?[0-9]+$/ { c += ($2 < 0 ? -$2 : $2); v += $3; n++ }
		END { if (n) printf "%.1f mA %.3f V (%d samples)", c / n / 1000, v / n / 1e6, n; else printf "NA" }' "$out"
}
snap() {
	qstats >"$dir/qstats.$1" || { log 'FAIL qcom_stats read'; exit 1; }
	cat "$stats/ddr_stats" >"$dir/ddr.$1" || { log 'FAIL ddr_stats read'; exit 1; }
	for required in ddr cxsd aosd; do
		grep -Eq "^$required Count: [0-9]+ .*Duration: [0-9]+" "$dir/qstats.$1" ||
			{ log "FAIL missing qcom_stats $required counter"; exit 1; }
	done
	grep -Eq '^DDR LPM .*count:[0-9]+' "$dir/ddr.$1" || { log 'FAIL missing DDR LPM counters'; exit 1; }
	cat /proc/interrupts >"$dir/irq.$1"
	awk 'NR > 1 { print $1, $2, $3, $4 }' /sys/kernel/debug/wakeup_sources >"$dir/ws.$1" 2>/dev/null
	for r in /sys/class/remoteproc/remoteproc*; do
		[ -d "$r" ] && printf '%s %s %s\n' "${r##*/}" "$(rd "$r/name")" "$(rd "$r/state")"
	done >"$dir/rproc.$1"
	if [ -r "$vxdir/vx" ]; then
		cat "$vxdir/vx" >"$dir/vx.$1" 2>&1
		cat "$vxdir/vx_raw" >"$dir/vx_raw.$1" 2>&1
	fi
	[ "$battmgr" = 0 ] || battery >"$dir/battery.$1"
	printf '%s %s\n' "$(frozen)" "$(cluster_counts)" >"$dir/apss.$1"
}

{
	echo "kernel=$(uname -r)"
	echo "bisect_dtb=$(tr -d '\000' 2>/dev/null <"${ROG5_BISECT_DT:-/proc/device-tree}/rog5,standby-bisect" || echo none)"
	echo "bisect_base=$(tr -d '\000' 2>/dev/null <"${ROG5_BISECT_DT:-/proc/device-tree}/rog5,standby-bisect-base" || echo none)"
	echo "cmdline=$(cat /proc/cmdline)"
	echo "secs=$secs battmgr=$battmgr arm_vx=$arm_vx ddr_log_off=$ddr_log_off"
	echo "mem_sleep=$(rd /sys/power/mem_sleep)"
	echo "cpuidle_governor=$(rd /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpuidle/current_governor_ro)"
} >"$dir/meta.env"
# Providers still holding their boot votes (sync_state not reached, e.g. a
# consumer that never probes) would keep CX/DDR up and confound the trial.
find "${ROG5_BISECT_SYSDEV:-/sys/devices}" -maxdepth 8 -name state_synced 2>/dev/null | while read -r f; do
	[ "$(rd "$f")" = 1 ] || echo "${f%/state_synced}"
done >"$dir/unsynced"
log "result directory $dir"
cursor=$(journalctl -n0 --show-cursor -o cat 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/^-- cursor: //p')

awake_before=NA
[ "$battmgr" = 0 ] || awake_before=$(sample_current 10 "$dir/current.before")
if [ "$ddr_log_off" = 1 ]; then
	[ -w "$qmp" ] || { log 'FAIL --ddr-log-off needs the rog5-aop-qmp module'; exit 1; }
	echo '{class: ddr, res: ddr_log, val: 0}' >"$qmp" || { log 'FAIL ddr_log QMP message refused'; exit 1; }
	log 'sent {class: ddr, res: ddr_log, val: 0}'
fi
if [ "$arm_vx" = 1 ]; then
	[ -w "$qmp" ] || { log 'FAIL --arm-vx needs the rog5-aop-qmp module'; exit 1; }
	echo '{class: lpm_mon, type: cxpc, dur: 1000, flush: 5, ts_adj: 1}' >"$qmp" ||
		{ log 'FAIL lpm_mon QMP message refused'; exit 1; }
fi
snap before
b0=$(boot)
s0=$(rd "$succ_file")
case $s0 in ''|*[!0-9]*) log 'FAIL suspend counter unavailable'; exit 1 ;; esac
log "suspending for $secs s"
# Never suspend without a wake alarm (review 2026-09-29).
rtcwake -m no -s "$secs" >/dev/null || { log 'FAIL rtcwake could not arm the RTC; not suspending'; exit 1; }
systemctl suspend --check-inhibitors=no || { log 'FAIL suspend request refused'; exit 1; }
i=0
while [ "$(rd "$succ_file")" = "$s0" ] && [ "$i" -lt $((secs + 90)) ]; do sleep 1; i=$((i + 1)); done
sleep 3
b1=$(boot)
snap after
awake_after=NA
[ "$battmgr" = 0 ] || awake_after=$(sample_current 10 "$dir/current.after")
[ -z "$cursor" ] || journalctl --after-cursor="$cursor" -k -o short-monotonic --no-pager >"$dir/kmsg" 2>/dev/null

# -- summary
s1=$(rd "$succ_file")
case $s1 in ''|*[!0-9]*) log 'FAIL suspend counter unavailable'; exit 1 ;; esac
# APSS: seconds timekeeping stayed frozen; s2idle requests and PSCI refusals
# of cluster-sleep-1 (the refusals include awake idle in the window).
set -- $(cat "$dir/apss.before") $(cat "$dir/apss.after")
apss_s=$(awk -v a="$1" -v b="$5" 'BEGIN { if (a ~ /^-?[0-9]+[.][0-9]+$/ && b ~ /^-?[0-9]+[.][0-9]+$/) printf "%.1f", b - a; else print "NA" }')
apss_n=NA apss_rej=NA
case $4$8 in *[!0-9]*|'') ;; *) apss_n=$(($8 - $4)) ;; esac
case $3$7 in *[!0-9]*|'') ;; *) apss_rej=$(($7 - $3)) ;; esac
{
	echo "ROG5 standby bisect: $(sed -n 's/^bisect_dtb=//p' "$dir/meta.env") on $(sed -n 's/^bisect_base=//p' "$dir/meta.env"), kernel $(uname -r), $(date -u +%FT%TZ)"
	echo "suspends: $s0 -> $s1 (window $(awk -v a="$b0" -v b="$b1" 'BEGIN { printf "%.0f", b - a }') s boot clock)"
	echo "wake: $(rd /sys/power/pm_wakeup_irq) ($(grep -h -m1 -E 'PM: suspend exit|Triggering wakeup|wakeup from' "$dir/kmsg" 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-120))"
	echo
	echo 'qcom_stats deltas (entries, seconds asleep; 19.2 MHz ticks):'
	join "$dir/qstats.before" "$dir/qstats.after" 2>/dev/null | awk '{
		n = 0; for (i = 2; i <= NF; i++) {
			if ($i == "Count:") c[n] = $(i + 1)
			if ($i == "Duration:") { d[n] = $(i + 1); n++ } }
		if (n == 2) printf "  %-12s +%d  %.1f s\n", $1, c[1] - c[0], (d[1] - d[0]) / 19200000 }'
	echo 'subsystems with no SMEM counter (never started, or not published): '"$(awk 'NF == 1 { printf "%s ", $1 }' "$dir/qstats.after")"
	echo
	echo 'ddr_stats deltas:'
	ddr_deltas | awk -F '\t' '$2 != 0 || $3 != 0 || /LPM/ { printf "  %-28s +%.0f  %.1f s\n", $1, $2, $3 / 19200000 }'
	echo
	if [ -f "$dir/vx.after" ]; then
		echo 'AOP violators (rog5-sleep-blockers/vx; stale unless --arm-vx):'
		sed 's/^/  /' "$dir/vx.after" | head -n 20
	else
		echo 'AOP violators: rog5-sleep-blockers not loaded (vx not read)'
	fi
	echo
	if [ "$battmgr" = 1 ]; then
		echo "battery awake before: $awake_before; after: $awake_after"
		awk -F= -v s="$(awk -v a="$b0" -v b="$b1" 'BEGIN { print b - a }')" '
			FNR == 1 { f++ } $1 == "charge_counter" { q[f] = $2 }
			END { if (q[1] ~ /^[0-9]+$/ && q[2] ~ /^[0-9]+$/ && s >= 5)
				printf "charge_counter %d -> %d uAh: %.2f mAh over %.0f s = %.0f mA average (pack; ~1 mAh resolution, awake part included)\n",
					q[1], q[2], (q[1] - q[2]) / 1000, s, (q[1] - q[2]) / 1000 / s * 3600 }' \
			"$dir/battery.before" "$dir/battery.after"
	else
		echo 'battery: no battmgr in this boot (noadsp): counters only'
	fi
	echo
	echo 'remoteprocs after:'; sed 's/^/  /' "$dir/rproc.after"
	echo 'wakeup_sources with new events:'
	awk 'NR == FNR { a[$1] = $3; next } ($3 - a[$1]) > 0 { printf "  %s +%d\n", $1, $3 - a[$1] }' \
		"$dir/ws.before" "$dir/ws.after" 2>/dev/null
	echo
	lpm=$(ddr_deltas | awk -F '\t' '/LPM/ { n += $2; s += $3 } END { printf "%d %.1f\n", n, s / 19200000 }')
	lpm_s=${lpm#* } lpm=${lpm% *}
	set -- $(qdelta ddr); ddr_count=$1 ddr_s=$2
	set -- $(qdelta cxsd); cx_count=$1 cx_s=$2
	echo "APSS asleep: timekeeping frozen $apss_s s (must cover most of the $secs s), cluster-sleep-1 s2idle requests +$apss_n, PSCI refusals +$apss_rej (software view; the RPMh counters above are the hardware view)"
	# Awake idle in the few seconds around the suspend also counts refusals.
	[ "$apss_rej" = NA ] || [ "$apss_n" = NA ] || [ "$apss_rej" -lt "$apss_n" ] ||
		echo "WARN PSCI refused cluster-sleep-1 +$apss_rej times against +$apss_n s2idle requests: check the RPMh counters before trusting this trial"
	if [ -s "$dir/unsynced" ]; then
		echo "WARN providers without sync_state (boot votes kept; trial confounded):"
		sed 's/^/  /' "$dir/unsynced"
	fi
	if [ "$((s1 - s0))" -ne 1 ]; then
		echo "VERDICT invalid: expected exactly one successful suspend (got $((s1 - s0)))"
	elif [ "$apss_s" = NA ] || awk -v a="$apss_s" -v s="$secs" 'BEGIN { exit !(a < 0.8 * s) }'; then
		echo "VERDICT invalid: timekeeping frozen only $apss_s s of $secs s (early wake?)"
	elif [ "$apss_n" = NA ] || [ "$apss_n" -lt 1 ]; then
		echo "VERDICT invalid: the cluster never requested its APSS-off state in s2idle (+$apss_n)"
	elif [ "$ddr_count" -gt 0 ] && [ "$lpm" -gt 0 ] && [ "$cx_count" -gt 0 ]; then
		echo "VERDICT POSITIVE (repeat against a matched baseline): qcom_stats ddr +$ddr_count ($ddr_s s), ddr_stats LPM +$lpm ($lpm_s s), cxsd +$cx_count ($cx_s s)"
	elif [ "$ddr_count" -gt 0 ] || [ "$lpm" -gt 0 ] || [ "$cx_count" -gt 0 ]; then
		echo "VERDICT PARTIAL (not corroborated by all three counters): qcom_stats ddr +$ddr_count ($ddr_s s), ddr_stats LPM +$lpm ($lpm_s s), cxsd +$cx_count ($cx_s s)"
	else
		echo "VERDICT negative: no DDR LPM (qcom_stats ddr +$ddr_count, ddr_stats LPM +$lpm), cxsd +$cx_count"
	fi
} >"$dir/summary.txt"
cat "$dir/summary.txt"
